viewpie (0.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Close every buffer handle behind a hardware-decoded frame. On a Pi 5 the
    HEVC decoder hands out luma and chroma separately, and the chroma leaked
    on every reconnect, resume and fullscreen switch until feeds no longer
    came back.
  * A panic in any thread restarts the wall, rather than leaving a camera
    frozen or a paused wall paused for good.

 -- Sebastian Noack <sebastian.noack@gmail.com>  Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

viewpie (0.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. A camera wall for a Raspberry Pi: RTSP cameras decoded
    with ffmpeg, in hardware where the board has a decoder for the codec, and
    every viewport put on screen in one atomic KMS commit, so each advances
    at its camera's own rate.
  * Cameras are named once and shown wherever a viewport names them, in a
    grid or a drawn layout, on one display or two; a camera shown in several
    places is decoded once. A viewport may rotate through several cameras.
  * A camera that drops out is reconnected on a backoff, and its viewport
    goes dark meanwhile. A stream larger than the display can show is
    refused as it connects.
  * With pause_off_screen, the cameras are disconnected while a display is
    unplugged, or its television is in standby or on another input, which
    the television says over HDMI-CEC.
  * The television's remote drives the wall over HDMI-CEC: left and right
    step the rotating viewports, down and up show one camera fullscreen and
    go through the others, back returns to the grid, as does ten minutes
    with nothing pressed. A camera may give a sharper stream for fullscreen
    as fullscreen_url.
  * Runs as its own unprivileged user, from the Debian package or the
    container image.

 -- Sebastian Noack <sebastian.noack@gmail.com>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
